GrimbiXcode/mtgscan
https://github.com/GrimbiXcode/mtgscan
License: GPL-3.0 (repo's committed LICENSE.md is the GNU GPLv3 text, and
GitHub's license detector reports GPL-3.0 for this repo). NOTE: the
repo's own README states "MIT License" - that README claim does not
match the LICENSE.md file actually committed to the repo. Treat this
project as GPL-3.0 for any future reuse; do not rely on the README.

Because GPL-3.0 is copyleft, no code, snippets, or line-level structure
from this repository were copied into this project - only the general
architectural approach (which corner to crop, running OCR against a few
crop variants and scoring the results, using brightness/hue variance as
a foil signal) was studied and re-derived independently. Algorithms and
ideas are not themselves protected by copyright; only a work's specific
expression is, so this does not place the surrounding project under
GPL-3.0. It is credited here as the source of the architectural approach.

Informed:
  - Collector-number crop strategy (frontend/src/features/scanner/ocr/collectorNumberRegion.ts):
    fixed-position corner crops instead of full-frame card segmentation.
  - Multi-strategy OCR fallback with early-exit scoring (frontend/src/features/scanner/ocr/ocrFallback.ts),
    conceptually similar to their `performCollectorNumberOCRWithFallback`.
  - Foil-detection heuristic (frontend/src/features/scanner/ocr/foilDetect.ts),
    conceptually similar to their `detectFoilCard` (brightness/hue variance, no ML).

